            <p class="eyebrow">A faculty field guide</p>
            <h1 id="page-title">Online teaching, designed for belonging.</h1>
            <p class="hero-lede">A strong online course is not a digital filing cabinet. It is a clear, human learning environment where students know where to go, what matters, and how to keep moving.</p>
            <div class="button-row">
              <a class="button button-primary" href="#practices">Explore the practices</a>
              <a class="button button-secondary" href="#weekly">Plan next week</a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <aside class="first-moves" aria-labelledby="first-moves-title">
            <p class="kicker">Start small</p>
            <h2 id="first-moves-title">Three moves with an outsized return</h2>
            <ol>
              <li><strong>Orient.</strong> Show students exactly how this week works.</li>
              <li><strong>Connect.</strong> Make your teaching presence visible and useful.</li>
              <li><strong>Respond.</strong> Give feedback students can act on next.</li>
            </ol>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </section>

